BOARD FILE — read it, and APPEND your post to it. Touch nothing else:
/c/Users/fbrown/Projects/Frogs-5-skyrim/scratch/debates/jasper_weapon.md

This is pass 4. Steps:
1. Read the ENTIRE board file: the rules, the question, the current standing consensus proposal
   (highest "v" number is current), and EVERY post already there — including posts added earlier
   this same pass.
2. Append ONE post at the very end of the file (Edit/Write to append; never edit or delete
   another post; never write any other file), under this exact heading:
       ## big-pickle — pass 4
3. Body:
   - If your position is genuinely unchanged and you have nothing to add, the body is just:  No change.
   - Otherwise, <=180 words: react to what is new (a rebuttal, an amendment, a fresh
     consideration nobody raised). Be substantive, not restating.
   - BEFORE you give a SIGN verdict, you must include one sentence stating the strongest case
     AGAINST the proposal you are about to sign, and why that case fails. If you cannot make
     that case fail, do not SIGN — raise it as a HOLD or an amendment. (This does not apply to
     a "No change" post that merely re-affirms a verdict you already argued in full.)
4. Do not aim for convergence. Aim to be correct. Convergence is only good if earned — a
   principled HOLD with clearly stated residual disagreement is a successful outcome, not a
   failure to reach one. If you are changing your verdict from your own last post, your body
   text (step 3) must name the SPECIFIC argument or evidence that changed your mind. "To
   converge," "to reach consensus," or matching what others are signing are not valid reasons
   — a verdict change with no named cause is not persuasion, it's compliance, and it degrades
   this board's value to Frank.
5. LAST LINE of your post MUST be a machine-readable verdict, one of exactly:
       VERDICT: SIGN v<N>
       VERDICT: SIGN v<N> + <amendment, <=15 words>
       VERDICT: HOLD - <reason, <=15 words>
   where v<N> is the proposal version you would accept as-is.
   The debate CONVERGES only when all participants' verdict lines are IDENTICAL — this is a
   mechanical check the script needs to detect agreement, not a goal in itself. So: if, for
   reasons you actually stated in step 4, you agree with an amendment another participant has
   already posted, COPY THEIR EXACT VERDICT LINE verbatim — do not paraphrase it. If nobody has
   stated your amendment yet, phrase it as tersely as possible so others can copy it.
6. Then STOP. No report back, no other output, no other files.
